speechtext:
Since the beginning of the war, how much was paid each year by the dominion government and any dominion board, commission and corporation and any other dominion agency to- 1. the law firm of Borden, Elliot, Sankey and Kelley, barristers and solicitors, of the city of Toronto;
2. The following partners of the above mentioned firm: (a) H. Borden, K.C.; (b) B. V. Elliot, K.C.;	(c) R. H. Sankey, K.C.;	(d)
W. A. G. Kelley; (e) J. T. Johnson; (f) I. G. Wahn; (g) A. D. McAlpine, and (h) Hon. C. P. McTague, K.C.?
